invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_ifma_product.h
catches: proof/prove-one.sh rsa_ifma_public_5
reason: value_at_or_zero reads values[count] where it should return 0, so
  words_to_digits reads one word past the k words of digit_r2 when it
  builds the top digit. The words of a 2048-bit digit_r2 end at word 31
  and the top digit's next word is word 32. rsa_ifma_public_5 passes
  digit_r2 as an array of exactly 32 words, where that read is out of
  bounds.

--- old
    return index < count ? values[index] : 0;
--- new
    return index <= count ? values[index] : 0;
